# =====================================================================
# OpenSSL 3.x AES-GCM false positive
# =====================================================================
#
# OpenSSL 3.0.5+ emits "Conditional jump or move depends on
# uninitialised value(s)" warnings from the AES-GCM assembly
# implementation on x86_64 (release builds with assembly enabled).
#
# The hand-written assembly reads padding/alignment bytes that
# valgrind considers uninitialized, but the values are never used
# in a way that affects correctness.  This is a well-known valgrind
# limitation with optimized crypto assembly, NOT a bug in OpenSSL
# or TH8.
#
# TH8 encounters this in the secure variable subsystem
# (th8_secure.c), which uses AES-256-GCM for encrypted-at-rest
# variable storage.  The decryption path triggers the warning
# when EVP_DecryptFinal_ex validates the GCM authentication tag.
#
# References:
#   https://github.com/openssl/openssl/issues/19719
#   https://github.com/openssl/openssl/issues/8460
#

{
   openssl3_aes_gcm_cond
   Memcheck:Cond
   obj:*/libcrypto.so*
   ...
   obj:*/libcrypto.so*
}
